    {
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Entities newly unavailable (24h)",
      "description": "Entities that are unavailable now AND were available 24h ago — the only count here that carries new information. The previous panel counted raw hass_entity_available == 0, which measured 168 on 2026-08-21 and 168 six hours earlier: a number that never reaches zero and never changes is not a health indicator, and a permanently red panel gets ignored. Much of that 168 is entities that are SUPPOSED to be absent — a sleeping car, unlicensed camera features, out-of-range beacons, Z-Wave diagnostics that only populate when something breaks. See mjs-ha#81. Caveat: if Prometheus loses more than 24h of history this reads 0 rather than unknown; the HA reachable panel beside this one is the guard for that.",
      "id": 46,
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 4,
        "x": 4,
        "y": 33
      },
