        },
        "textMode": "auto",
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "justifyMode": "center"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "yellow",
                "value": 1
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 5
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "short",
          "noValue": "0",
          "mappings": [],
          "links": [
            {
              "title": "Home Assistant",
              "url": "https://ha.nerdsbythehour.com/",
              "targetBlank": true
            }
          ]
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "count((hass_entity_available == 0) and (hass_entity_available offset 24h == 1)) or vector(0)",
          "instant": true,
          "legendFormat": "",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Safety entities down",
      "description": "The alarm panel and the door contacts it arms on. Mirrors the two alerting rules exactly: an entity reported unavailable by its integration, OR a device whose own heartbeat (device temperature, link quality, uptime) has not reported in 24h. Previously this counted staleness on the door contacts themselves, which was a false positive by construction — HA's last_updated only advances when state CHANGES, so a closed door that stays closed never updates however healthy the sensor is. That expression read 4 on 2026-08-21 with all four devices demonstrably alive. Both signals are kept because availability alone reads 1 for unknown after a restart (mjs-ha#69) and staleness alone cries wolf. See mj-infra-flux#182.",
